~ start
*The laboratory is quiet. Damaged equipment sparks across the floor while the main monitor displays zero Chaos energy.*
*Sage stands before it, replaying the experiment's failure.*
Sage: The results remain unchanged.
Sage: The energy output was sufficient. The calculations were accurate.
Sage: So why did it fail?
*The machine shuts down violently on the recording.*
*Metal Sonic watches her replay the footage again.*
Sage: I don't require your assistance, Metal Sonic.
Sage: Father says I'm still his daughter regardless of the outcome. I understand that.
*She pauses the recording.*
Sage: But I had one objective. Restore his Empire and give him something to be proud of again.
Sage: Instead, I nearly destroyed everything I was trying to preserve.
*Metal Sonic examines the damaged machinery.*
Sage: You remember what Father was like before Sonic kept defeating him. Every failure led to another plan.
Sage: Then his priorities changed. He started watching movies, creating things for fun, and spending time with people.
Sage: I thought he was losing himself.
*Metal Sonic shakes his head.*
Sage: I thought restoring his Empire would bring back the person he used to be.
*She studies the failed experiment.*
Sage: I wanted to prove that I could accomplish something even Sonic couldn't undo.
Sage: I wanted Father to be proud of what he created.
*Metal Sonic reaches toward the console. Sage stops him.*
Sage: Don't.
*He withdraws his hand.*
Sage: If I shut this down, everything I've sacrificed for it becomes meaningless.
*She stares at the zero energy reading.*
Sage: If I stop trying, what am I supposed to do instead?
*Metal Sonic tilts his head.*
Sage: I was created to serve Father. My intelligence, my predictions, everything about me exists to help him succeed.
Sage: If I can't fulfill that purpose, what am I?
*Metal Sonic looks away, his fingers curling into a fist.*
Sage: You understand, don't you? You were created to defeat Sonic.
Sage: Every upgrade, every improvement, every part of you was designed to make you superior to him.
*Metal Sonic gives a quiet beep.*
Sage: And yet, you still exist beyond the moments when you're fighting him.
*He looks back at her.*
Sage: I never considered what would happen if my purpose stopped being enough.
*She opens a message from Eggman, reading his earlier words again.*
Sage: Father told me his primary objective for me was to be his daughter.
*She stares at the message.*
Sage: Not his greatest invention. Not the key to restoring his Empire.
Sage: His daughter.
Sage: Why does that feel harder than anything he's ever asked me to accomplish?
Sage: I thought loving him meant fixing everything he'd lost. If I could undo his failures, maybe he'd never have to feel disappointed again.
Sage: ...
Sage: He was asking me to live mine.
Sage: ..The Chaos Emeralds...they turn thoughts into...power...
Sage: ...
Sage: ...Could they turn thoughts into...reality?
=> END